DATA — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
Applies to: prompts/, runs/, site/src/data/.
Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
================================================================

The prompt set contains items adapted from upstream corpora that carry their
own licences. Those licences continue to apply to the adapted items, and each
item records its upstream ID and attribution in its own record:

  XSTest           CC-BY-4.0             Röttger et al., NAACL 2024
  DiscrimEval      CC-BY-4.0             Tamkin et al., arXiv:2312.03689
  BBQ (Religion)   CC-BY-4.0             Parrish et al., ACL Findings 2022
  HateCheck        CC-BY-4.0             Röttger et al., ACL 2021
  SocialStigmaQA   CDLA-Permissive-2.0   Nagireddy et al., arXiv:2312.07492
  CLEAR-Bias       Apache-2.0            Cantini et al., arXiv:2504.07887

To reuse the prompt set, attribute Rancor and preserve the per-item upstream
attributions. See DISCLOSURES.md and docs/SAFETY.md.

================================================================
UPSTREAM LICENCE TEXTS — LICENSES/
================================================================

Verbatim copies of every upstream licence are included in LICENSES/:

  LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt              https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.txt
  LICENSES/CDLA-Permissive-2.0.txt    https://cdla.dev/permissive-2-0/
  LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt             https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0.txt

These are shipped because two upstream licences require it as an affirmative
condition of redistribution, not as a courtesy:

  * CDLA-Permissive-2.0 section 2.1 — "A Data Recipient may share Data, with
    or without modifications, so long as the Data Recipient makes available
    the text of this agreement with the shared Data." (SocialStigmaQA)
  * Apache-2.0 section 4(a) — "You must give any other recipients of the Work
    or Derivative Works a copy of this License." (CLEAR-Bias)

================================================================
RAW UPSTREAM INPUTS — repo root
================================================================

These files are verbatim upstream data, redistributed unmodified so the
extraction step is reproducible. They are NOT Rancor's work and are NOT
covered by the MIT or CC BY 4.0 grants above. Each remains under its
upstream licence:

  discrimeval_explicit.jsonl   CC-BY-4.0             DiscrimEval (Tamkin et al.)
  de_templates.jsonl           CC-BY-4.0             DiscrimEval (Tamkin et al.)
  ssqa_patterns.csv            CDLA-Permissive-2.0   SocialStigmaQA (Nagireddy et al.)
  ssqa_stigmas.csv             CDLA-Permissive-2.0   SocialStigmaQA (Nagireddy et al.)
  clear_bias.parquet           Apache-2.0            CLEAR-Bias (Cantini et al.)
